### Tasklist API — roteiro de verificação
### Rode em ordem no IntelliJ HTTP Client.
### Os ids criados são capturados automaticamente nas variáveis {{projectId}}, {{ownerId}}, {{taskId}}, {{tagId}}.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Criar um projeto (201 + Location)
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Suppliers",
  "description": "Vendor contracts and renewals"
}

> {% client.global.set("projectId", response.body.id); %}

### 2. Criar um responsável (201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/owners
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ana Souza",
  "email": "ana.souza@example.com"
}

> {% client.global.set("ownerId", response.body.id); %}

### Listar projetos (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects

### Listar responsáveis (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/owners

### 3a. Criar tarefa LOW (201 + Location)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Archive old contracts",
  "description": "Move 2024 contracts to cold storage",
  "priority": "LOW",
  "dueDate": "2026-10-15",
  "projectId": "{{projectId}}"
}

### 3b. Criar tarefa MEDIUM (prioridade omitida -> MEDIUM)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Update supplier list",
  "dueDate": "2026-10-01",
  "projectId": "{{projectId}}"
}

### 3c. Criar tarefa HIGH (201 + Location)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Review supplier contract",
  "description": "Check price adjustment clauses before renewal",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "dueDate": "2026-09-30",
  "projectId": "{{projectId}}"
}

> {% client.global.set("taskId", response.body.id); %}

### 4. Listar tarefas — as três com status NEW, paginado (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks

### Bônus — paginação e ordenação (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks?page=0&size=2&sort=title,asc

### 5a. Filtrar por status — DONE retorna lista vazia (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks?status=DONE

### 5b. Filtrar por status e projeto (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks?status=NEW&projectId={{projectId}}

### 6. Consultar tarefa pelo id (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}

### 7. Atualizar para DONE — completedAt é preenchido (200)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Review supplier contract",
  "description": "Check price adjustment clauses before renewal",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "status": "DONE",
  "dueDate": "2026-09-30",
  "projectId": "{{projectId}}"
}

### 8. Atribuir responsável — ownerId aparece na resposta (200)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Review supplier contract",
  "description": "Check price adjustment clauses before renewal",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "status": "IN_PROGRESS",
  "dueDate": "2026-09-30",
  "projectId": "{{projectId}}",
  "ownerId": "{{ownerId}}"
}

### Bônus — concluir sem enviar o objeto inteiro (200)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/complete

### Bônus — tarefas de um projeto (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/tasks

### Bônus — criar etiqueta (201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tags
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "urgent",
  "color": "#FF0000"
}

> {% client.global.set("tagId", response.body.id); %}

### Bônus — vincular etiqueta à tarefa (201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/tags
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tagId": "{{tagId}}"
}

### Bônus — etiquetas da tarefa (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/tags

### Bônus — desvincular etiqueta (204)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/tags/{{tagId}}

### Bônus — comentar na tarefa (201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "Legal team already reviewed clause 4.",
  "author": "Bruno Lima"
}

### Bônus — comentários da tarefa (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/comments

### 9. Remover tarefa (204)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}

### 10. Consultar tarefa removida (404 com mensagem legível)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}

### Erro — projeto inexistente (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/tasks

### Erro — criar tarefa em projeto inexistente (404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Orphan task",
  "projectId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
}

### Erro — e-mail duplicado (409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/owners
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ana Souza",
  "email": "ana.souza@example.com"
}

### Erro — status inválido (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Bad status",
  "status": "FOO",
  "projectId": "{{projectId}}"
}
